This site measures how often an NCAA volleyball team wins after losing the first set, then compares that result with attack totals from a larger beach-volleyball dataset.

Teams that lose the first set still win about 21.2% of NCAA Division I matches overall. Comeback chances rise dramatically as matches extend to four or five sets.



&lt;strong&gt;21.2%&lt;/strong&gt;
Overall comeback rate after losing set 1


&lt;strong&gt;0%&lt;/strong&gt;
3-set matches


&lt;strong&gt;33.2%&lt;/strong&gt;
4-set matches


&lt;strong&gt;51.5%&lt;/strong&gt;
5-set matches

